{"t": 546.52, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 2, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "sece_full", "rationale": "Previous SSHI+FBR designs failed because the full-bridge diode drops (0.5V) are too significant given the low open-circuit voltage (3.2V) of the piezo, and the large storage capacitor slowed startup. I am replacing the rectifier with a Synchronous Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) topology. Using two inductors and two switches, the circuit extracts charge at both the positive and negative voltage extrema. This eliminates diode drops entirely, significantly increasing the delivered power and reducing the startup time. I will also use a smaller storage capacitor (4.7 uF) to ensure fast startup while maintaining low ripple.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "sece_full", "rationale": "Previous SSHI+FBR designs failed because the full-bridge diode drops (0.5V) are too significant given the low open-circuit voltage (3.2V) of the piezo, and the large storage capacitor slowed startup. I am replacing the rectifier with a Synchronous Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) topology. Using two inductors and two switches, the circuit extracts charge at both the positive and negative voltage extrema. This eliminates diode drops entirely, significantly increasing the delivered power and reducing the startup time. I will also use a smaller storage capacitor (4.7 uF) to ensure fast startup while maintaining low ripple.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.01}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 0.0001, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "pos"}, {"id": "L2", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzn", "n2"], "value": 0.01}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "G2", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 0.0001, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "neg"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 4.7e-06}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0",